>> title: Refried Beans, Instant Pot
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: beans, pinto, mexican, side, instant pot, pressure cooker, no soak
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> aka: instant pot refried beans, pressure cooker pinto beans, instant pot pinto beans, no soak pinto beans, frijoles refritos, refried pintos
>> servings: 8
>> dish: refried-beans
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas
>> time: 1 hr 40 min
>> slack: unforgiving — a pinto that is only just cooked mashes grainy, and there is no rescuing it once it is in the fat
>> washing-up: the Instant Pot, a colander to drain the beans, a bowl to catch the cooking liquid
>> keeps: 4 days — they set firm cold and loosen with fat and water in the pan, which is how they were made

>> step: cook the pintos from dry, no soak — 40 min at high pressure
Put @dried pinto beans{1%lb}(450 g; dry, not soaked) into the #Instant Pot{} with @water{6%cups}(1.4 L), @white onion{1/2%large}(halved), @garlic{4%cloves} and @bay leaf{1}, lock the lid and ~pressure cook{40%min} at high pressure.

>> step: wait out the natural release 20 min, drain but keep the liquid
Let @&(~1)pot{} ~natural release{20%min} until the pin drops, then drain the beans and keep the cooking liquid — the mash is loosened with it. Pull the onion and the bay leaf.

>> step: fry the onion in lard 6 min
Fry @yellow onion{1%small}(finely chopped) in @lard{1/3%cup}(70 g; or bacon fat) in the emptied inner pot on the highest Sauté setting ~fry{6%min}, until it is soft and the fat smells of it.

>> step: mash the beans in
Add @&(~2)beans{} to @&(~1)onion{} with a cup of their cooking liquid and mash with a #potato masher{}, straight in the pot.

>> step: fry down 10 min until it holds a line
Fry @&(~1)beans{} on Sauté, stirring, until thick enough to hold a line, ~fry{10%min}, with @kosher salt{2 1/2%tsp} and @ground cumin{1/2%tsp}.
